"""Detect comment-opening punctuation, with small separator/heading responses.

A hash is strong in Python-looking or indented code, but weak in prose and
links. Double slashes favor indentation and recent source-code syntax too.
Escaped source listings and numbered listings receive weaker responses.
A 600-character buffer supplies these surface cues, resetting per document.
